  "vo": "Nurse paycheck versus the median house. Median nurse pay: ninety-seven five fifty. Take-home, every two weeks: twenty-nine seventy-nine. Same four envelopes. FUTURE, fifteen percent: four forty-seven. First-time buyers put ten percent down: forty-two nine. Call it forty-three grand over four fifty: ninety-six paychecks. Exact: ninety-six point oh three. Three years, eight months. That's if every FUTURE dollar goes to the house. Twenty percent down, to skip PMI? The median first-time buyer is now forty. Double the down payment. How old would you be? Seven point four years.",
